asr-001778
01:19:15.100 --> 01:19:25.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll ask the questions later on. Pero I want to ask the Secretary, with this Supreme Court ruling on the unprogrammed funds,

asr-001779
01:19:26.600 --> 01:19:34.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and narinig ko kanina sa nag-umpisa na kayo and your team to go through the Supreme Court ruling.

asr-001780
01:19:34.120 --> 01:19:38.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Makapal siya. I also went through it or tried to go through it this morning.

asr-001781
01:19:39.720 --> 01:19:44.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But what can you now... We're now in the thick of the budget process.

asr-001782
01:19:44.080 --> 01:19:56.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, sabi nga ng ating chairman, patapos na kami and we're going to enter into consolidation of the different budgets...

asr-001783
01:19:56.600 --> 01:20:02.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ...of different agencies. And then from there, magpa-plenary debates na kami.

asr-001784
01:20:02.020 --> 01:20:25.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So what are the recommendations of the DBM in relation to the Supreme Court ruling so that we can already fine-tune, we can already adjust, we can already watch out for kung merong mga kailangan kaming tignan mabuti.

asr-001785
01:20:25.920 --> 01:20:25.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-001786
01:20:26.600 --> 01:20:33.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang dapat naming i-adjust dito sa 2027 budget process.

asr-001787
01:20:34.520 --> 01:20:37.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Mr. Senate President.

asr-001788
01:20:37.940 --> 01:20:41.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: There are things that are indeed very clear in the decision.

asr-001789
01:20:41.680 --> 01:20:54.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And we are also happy to report that for one, when the Supreme Court ruled on the unconstitutionality of the SAGIP, we don't have SAGIP anymore even in the 2027 unprogrammed appropriations.

