asr-002984
01:50:36.400 --> 01:50:40.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Before they can get the funds, they should have been certified as cleared by the NTF-LCAC.

asr-002985
01:50:41.020 --> 01:50:48.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And the funds are supposed to maintain that status of being cleared.

asr-002986
01:50:48.880 --> 01:50:54.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To provide opportunities for these cleared baranggays to have more economic activities,

asr-002987
01:50:54.680 --> 01:50:57.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: more access to government services.

asr-002988
01:50:57.120 --> 01:50:57.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-002989
01:50:57.960 --> 01:51:03.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then, ang iniisip ko, kasi ang rational ko, dapat over time,

asr-002990
01:51:04.000 --> 01:51:06.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: pag nakiklear yung baranggay, sige, that's what I mean,

asr-002991
01:51:07.080 --> 01:51:09.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: magdi-deliver tayo ng economic activity,

asr-002992
01:51:09.960 --> 01:51:15.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: bumababa rin yung number of baranggays na nangangailangan ng ganitong pondo

asr-002993
01:51:15.120 --> 01:51:17.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: dahil may sarili na silang economic activity.

asr-002994
01:51:18.600 --> 01:51:19.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, Your Honor.

asr-002995
01:51:19.400 --> 01:51:26.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang punto ko kasi, it's a program that is meant to clear and eventually,

asr-002996
01:51:26.480 --> 01:51:37.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: wala na tayong mga baranggays that will be infested with itong mga communist terrorist group po, diba?

asr-002997
01:51:38.100 --> 01:51:39.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, that is the objective.

asr-002998
01:51:40.320 --> 01:51:44.660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, based on the universe that we have from NTF-LCAC,

asr-002999
01:51:44.760 --> 01:51:47.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: yung mga baranggay only received assistance once.

asr-003000
01:51:48.260 --> 01:51:48.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-003001
01:51:48.800 --> 01:51:51.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, hindi po sila incremental.

asr-003002
01:51:51.560 --> 01:51:55.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we're looking at a universe of 9,588.

asr-003003
01:51:56.060 --> 01:51:56.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kaya nga,

asr-003004
01:51:56.480 --> 01:51:58.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: sa aming pag-uusap with NTF-LCAC,

asr-003005
01:51:59.420 --> 01:52:01.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: after the 2027 proposal,

asr-003006
01:52:02.140 --> 01:52:07.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: may natitira na lamang pong 2,001 baranggays na we hope to cover for the 2028.

asr-003007
01:52:07.440 --> 01:52:13.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, by that time, we have already covered the 9,588 cleared baranggays

asr-003008
01:52:13.000 --> 01:52:19.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because the design was, this is a one-off, one-time financial assistance to these cleared baranggays.

asr-003009
01:52:19.680 --> 01:52:22.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero ganun ba yan? Tama ba itong baranggay?

asr-003010
01:52:22.260 --> 01:52:26.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The way I understand it, the baranggay receives the same amount?

asr-003011
01:52:26.480 --> 01:52:27.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, one-time lang siya?

asr-003012
01:52:28.600 --> 01:52:29.540
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: One-time lang siya.

asr-003013
01:52:29.660 --> 01:52:30.400
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: One-time lang, sir.

asr-003014
01:52:30.680 --> 01:52:33.840
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Depende po dun sa budget na ibibigay for the year.

asr-003015
01:52:34.440 --> 01:52:34.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-003016
01:52:34.880 --> 01:52:37.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, ang natitira nilang is 2,000 baranggay, sabi nyo?

asr-003017
01:52:38.100 --> 01:52:39.520
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: 2,001 baranggays.

asr-003018
01:52:39.900 --> 01:52:45.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, kung every year nagbibigay ito ng 1,000 baranggay to 1,000 baranggays,

asr-003019
01:52:45.260 --> 01:52:48.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in two years, wala na tayong bibigyan?

asr-003020
01:52:49.620 --> 01:52:50.620
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Wala na po, sir.

asr-003021
01:52:51.340 --> 01:52:53.300
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Based on our record, sir.

asr-003022
01:52:53.740 --> 01:52:56.300
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Those are the totality of...

asr-003023
01:52:56.480 --> 01:52:59.280
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: baranggays that were cleared by the AIA.

asr-003024
01:52:59.760 --> 01:53:00.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay. Okay.

asr-003025
01:53:01.160 --> 01:53:05.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in two years, wala nang NTFK at ELCA?

asr-003026
01:53:05.700 --> 01:53:12.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The projection, Your Honor, is if we will be able to complete the remaining 2,001 baranggay sa 2028,

asr-003027
01:53:12.240 --> 01:53:13.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we should be finished by 2028.

asr-003028
01:53:14.200 --> 01:53:17.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: By 2028. So, complete na tayo. Tama ba yun?

asr-003029
01:53:17.580 --> 01:53:24.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, we will not see any more allocations to or appropriations to NTFK?

asr-003030
01:53:25.000 --> 01:53:26.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is also our understanding.

asr-003031
01:53:26.480 --> 01:53:30.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are understanding, Your Honor, because the universe has been set at 9,588 baranggays.

asr-003032
01:53:31.300 --> 01:53:35.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then every year, we give to 1,000 baranggays, diba?

asr-003033
01:53:35.380 --> 01:53:36.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1,000 to 2,000, Your Honor.

asr-003034
01:53:37.060 --> 01:53:39.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay. 1,000 to 2,000, depending on the budget. Okay.

asr-003035
01:53:40.700 --> 01:53:48.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, I'll hold you to that, Secretary, na by 2028, dapat wala nang...

asr-003036
01:53:49.180 --> 01:53:50.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 2028 should be the last.

asr-003037
01:53:50.820 --> 01:53:53.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The last. So, 2029, wala na.

asr-003038
01:53:53.320 --> 01:53:53.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-003039
01:53:54.600 --> 01:53:55.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-003040
01:53:55.320 --> 01:54:00.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We will be able to provide for the 9,500. That's the precedent, Your Honor.

asr-003041
01:54:00.260 --> 01:54:04.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, yes. And nakita ko naman, ganoon naman yung more or less, ganoon yung allocation na bibigay.

asr-003042
01:54:04.700 --> 01:54:05.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003043
01:54:05.520 --> 01:54:05.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Oo.

asr-003044
01:54:10.900 --> 01:54:13.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Tama ba, Director? Hindi kayo umiimik eh.

asr-003045
01:54:16.080 --> 01:54:21.880
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Actually, yun nga sabi ko nga, Your Honor, bumaba.

asr-003046
01:54:21.880 --> 01:54:23.880
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Kasi when we initially...

asr-003047
01:54:25.320 --> 01:54:31.860
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: initially had that BDP, it's 20 million in 2021.

asr-003048
01:54:32.340 --> 01:54:34.440
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Naging 4 million, 2022.

asr-003049
01:54:35.260 --> 01:54:37.340
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: 2023, naging 6 million.

asr-003050
01:54:37.960 --> 01:54:50.760
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: But right now, yun nga, as we discussed, yung 2027, I think 5 million yung na earmarked for this 1,948 baranggays.

asr-003051
01:54:51.480 --> 01:54:52.280
NTF-ELCAC Director for Planning and Production Alexander S. Umpar: Your Honor.

asr-003052
01:54:52.280 --> 01:54:54.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay. So, let me just repeat.

asr-003053
01:54:55.320 --> 01:55:03.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 2029, lahat ng baranggays na na-clear na, na binibigyan natin ng 10 million or 20?

asr-003054
01:55:04.060 --> 01:55:06.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Actually, it varies, Your Honor, depending on the budget.

asr-003055
01:55:06.820 --> 01:55:09.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But on the average, per baranggay, 20?

asr-003056
01:55:09.320 --> 01:55:11.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For 2027, we are at 5 million per baranggay.

asr-003057
01:55:11.840 --> 01:55:20.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 5 million per baranggay. We give them 5 million for socioeconomic development because na-clear na sila.

asr-003058
01:55:20.000 --> 01:55:25.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And the socioeconomic development is meant to make the baranggay...

asr-003059
01:55:25.320 --> 01:55:32.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: independent, economically viable, and then we go to the next baranggay.

asr-003060
01:55:33.620 --> 01:55:38.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, by 2029, clear na tayo. Wala na tayong dapat pondohan.

asr-003061
01:55:39.400 --> 01:55:43.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As far as the part of the LGSF is concerned, dapat wala na po.

asr-003062
01:55:43.760 --> 01:55:47.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Then, other agency budgets na lang, kung meron pa pong kailangan pagtuunan.

asr-003063
01:55:48.700 --> 01:55:50.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kasi meron ba tayong OPAPRU, eh?

asr-003064
01:55:50.340 --> 01:55:51.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor. Halimbawa po...

asr-003065
01:55:51.900 --> 01:55:54.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, yun ang aking proposal is to put the...

asr-003066
01:55:55.320 --> 01:56:06.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: LGSF-LCAP activities into OPAPRU para we only talk to one government agency dealing with peace and reconciliation.

asr-003067
01:56:07.100 --> 01:56:12.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi ang OPAPRU also dealing with the rebels' insurgency, eh? Insurgency.

asr-003068
01:56:13.760 --> 01:56:23.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meet, Your Honor, to the wisdom of the Senate if this item would be best lodged under OPAPRU, under the wisdom of the Senate.

asr-003069
01:56:23.400 --> 01:56:25.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: LGSF-LCAP naman is a task force, eh?

asr-003070
01:56:25.320 --> 01:56:26.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It is a whole-of-government task force.

asr-003071
01:56:27.040 --> 01:56:29.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, and OPAPRU's direction is the same.

asr-003072
01:56:30.000 --> 01:56:32.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, they're also building infrastructure projects.

asr-003073
01:56:32.540 --> 01:56:34.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: They're also giving socioeconomic packages.

asr-003074
01:56:35.260 --> 01:56:36.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-003075
01:56:36.320 --> 01:56:41.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The DBM naman po serves as administrator of this fund being an SPF.

asr-003076
01:56:41.220 --> 01:56:42.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we submit to the wisdom of the...

asr-003077
01:56:42.380 --> 01:56:50.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Well, in line with the optimization direction, Secretary, pakitingin na rin if we can merge it together.

asr-003078
01:56:50.840 --> 01:56:53.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, that's my proposal last year.

asr-003079
01:56:55.320 --> 01:57:01.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung Green-Green-Green program, Secretary, wala na this year, no?

asr-003080
01:57:02.480 --> 01:57:07.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For the Green-Green-Green, Your Honor, it was already integrated in the regular FALGO.

asr-003081
01:57:07.580 --> 01:57:12.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In the regular FALGO na. So, doon na siya. Before, it was a separate account, eh.

asr-003082
01:57:13.120 --> 01:57:21.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But we removed it in 2026 nga kasi it's hindi naman mandate ng DBM magpatayo ng parks, no?

asr-003083
01:57:21.940 --> 01:57:23.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, hindi nyo naman mandate yun.

asr-003084
01:57:25.320 --> 01:57:43.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Well, I'll go with my second round.

asr-003085
01:57:43.260 --> 01:57:49.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll let Senator Kiko give his questions first so I can review my notes.

asr-003086
01:57:49.560 --> 01:57:54.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. President. Magandang tanghali.

asr-003087
01:57:55.320 --> 01:58:08.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Secretary, actually, more of requests for updates and you don't have to answer these questions now, no?

asr-003088
01:58:08.120 --> 01:58:16.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But before plenary, if it can be, you can respond through your office and my staff.

asr-003089
01:58:16.180 --> 01:58:24.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But before that, Mr. President, I was listening intently on the discussions on the Supreme Court ruling.

asr-003090
01:58:24.420 --> 01:58:36.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And last week, actually, before it was announced, Justice Leonin and I were in the Senate Electoral Tribunal meeting.

asr-003091
01:58:36.560 --> 01:58:40.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And he gave us a preview of the ruling.

asr-003092
01:58:40.640 --> 01:58:51.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And he actually said that as far as 2024 and 2025 is concerned, the doctrine of post-operative fact will apply.

asr-003093
01:58:51.180 --> 01:58:53.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In other words, for future.

asr-003094
01:58:54.420 --> 01:58:58.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actions of both houses and the executive.

asr-003095
01:58:58.920 --> 01:59:01.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, hindi problema yun.

asr-003096
01:59:01.720 --> 01:59:05.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, ang kailangan siguro maklarify is yung 2026.

asr-003097
01:59:05.500 --> 01:59:18.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasi walang ganung, doon sa mga pondong nagastos na sa 2026, walang categorical statement on the doctrine of post-operative fact.

asr-003098
01:59:18.280 --> 01:59:19.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, I think you have to clarify that.

asr-003099
01:59:19.820 --> 01:59:23.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And having said that, do you have, of the 150,

asr-003100
01:59:24.420 --> 01:59:29.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: a billion for 2026, meron na bang narilis doon sa UNPROGRAM?

asr-003101
01:59:30.580 --> 01:59:37.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Your Honor, for the UNPROGRAM, the appropriations, we have not released any charge against Section 1A and 1B.

asr-003102
01:59:37.560 --> 01:59:37.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ah, okay.

asr-003103
01:59:38.060 --> 01:59:41.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Tanging foreign-assisted pa lamang po ang naririlis from UNPROGRAM.

asr-003104
01:59:41.100 --> 01:59:42.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, you won't have a problem, therefore.

asr-003105
01:59:43.060 --> 01:59:43.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-003106
01:59:44.180 --> 01:59:46.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you for that clarification.

asr-003107
01:59:47.400 --> 01:59:47.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now,

asr-003108
01:59:48.320 --> 01:59:52.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: my specific advocacies,

asr-003109
01:59:52.160 --> 01:59:54.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: actually, we wrote to the DPR,

asr-003110
01:59:54.440 --> 01:59:55.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: DBM on two matters.

asr-003111
01:59:56.100 --> 01:59:57.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This is the matter of the,

asr-003112
01:59:58.160 --> 01:59:59.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: right now kasi,

asr-003113
01:59:59.500 --> 02:00:00.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ah,

asr-003114
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:18.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Patuloy na namomblema yung livestock, particularly yung pork and piggery sector, yung magbababoy natin on the issue of the funding for the ASF.

asr-003115
02:00:18.420 --> 02:00:39.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So we wrote the DBM according to the DA. May mga unpaid ASF and avian influenza indemnities. 58.17 million and 336.9 million.

asr-003116
02:00:39.360 --> 02:00:48.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang recommendation ng DBM is to seek the President's approval to release 7.16 million.

asr-003117
02:00:48.420 --> 02:00:57.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: From the Contingency Fund and 329 million from the FY National Disaster Risk Reduction Fund.

asr-003118
02:00:58.620 --> 02:01:10.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So what is the status of the, after your recommendation, has the request of the approval been relayed to the President?

asr-003119
02:01:10.800 --> 02:01:15.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor. We have communicated formally our recommendation to the President.

asr-003120
02:01:16.100 --> 02:01:18.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And after this meeting, we'll communicate.

asr-003121
02:01:18.420 --> 02:01:28.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We'll communicate directly with the Office of the Executive Secretary to follow up on the status so that we can facilitate the immediate release of the allotments to DA to make sure that we'll be able to pay the farm.

asr-003122
02:01:28.620 --> 02:01:48.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you. And we will monitor that and I will ask that again during plenary because talagang tinatamaan ang ating livestock sector, particularly ang mga magbababoy dahil mas mababa na ang farmgate price sa production, cost of production.

asr-003123
02:01:48.420 --> 02:01:58.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the indemnities will go a long way for them given the current challenges.

asr-003124
02:01:58.620 --> 02:02:08.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We've also asked and we'll get a sense, the DA to consider asking the President to already declare a state of calamity.

asr-003125
02:02:09.180 --> 02:02:16.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Right now, five regions in the country have reported about 7 billion pesos losses in El Nino.

asr-003127
02:02:18.420 --> 02:02:24.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And it will get worse before it gets worse.

asr-003128
02:02:28.800 --> 02:02:44.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And so we would like to get the sense of the DBM Secretary. Would you support that declaration and would there be funds from the national government available?

asr-003129
02:02:45.240 --> 02:02:48.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Well, Your Honor, the declaration of a state.

asr-003130
02:02:48.420 --> 02:02:55.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of calamity arising from the extraordinary El Nino will not just unlock national government resources.

asr-003131
02:02:55.820 --> 02:02:59.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, it will also unlock local disaster risk reduction and management funds.

asr-003132
02:03:00.280 --> 02:03:12.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So for us to have a whole of government and whole of nation approach in responding to El Nino, certainly we would welcome, should the President declare a state of calamity,

asr-003133
02:03:12.520 --> 02:03:18.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we stand ready in guiding the agencies how they can best utilize their funding to respond to El Nino.

asr-003134
02:03:18.420 --> 02:03:19.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But do you have funds?

asr-003135
02:03:20.260 --> 02:03:29.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For El Nino, Your Honor, apart from the regular N-DREAM, the National Disaster Risk Reduction Management Fund,

asr-003136
02:03:29.800 --> 02:03:39.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: agencies have initially identified as well portions of their respective budgets that will be used for the preparation or response to El Nino.

asr-003137
02:03:39.080 --> 02:03:48.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Based on the data at hand, we have about 112 for the remaining part of the 2026 GAA, 112 billion.

asr-003138
02:03:48.420 --> 02:03:54.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And another 104 billion for the 2027 NEP.

asr-003139
02:03:54.340 --> 02:04:02.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is exclusive, Your Honor, of the Local Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Fund that may be accessed once there is this declaration.

asr-003140
02:04:03.060 --> 02:04:14.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But even absent, Your Honor, a national declaration, LGUs who have declared their respective state of calamity because of their mandate under Republic Act 10-121

asr-003141
02:04:14.760 --> 02:04:18.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: can already access their respective local disaster funds for this.

asr-003142
02:04:18.420 --> 02:04:21.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, may mga local declarations na.

asr-003143
02:04:21.980 --> 02:04:31.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In Regions 5, Calbar Zone, Region 2, Soxargen, and one more.

asr-003144
02:04:32.740 --> 02:04:33.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I forget.

asr-003145
02:04:33.700 --> 02:04:35.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Region 5. Did I say Region 5?

asr-003146
02:04:36.020 --> 02:04:36.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-003147
02:04:37.000 --> 02:04:41.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Region 2, Region 5, Calbar Zone, Soxargen, and Caraga.

asr-003148
02:04:42.340 --> 02:04:42.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: There you go.

asr-003149
02:04:42.920 --> 02:04:44.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So five have already locally.

asr-003150
02:04:44.400 --> 02:04:45.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But, you know.

asr-003151
02:04:46.300 --> 02:04:48.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So you're saying there is 120?

asr-003152
02:04:48.420 --> 02:04:50.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 122 billion for 2026.

asr-003153
02:04:51.480 --> 02:04:53.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 112 billion, Your Honor.

asr-003154
02:04:53.720 --> 02:04:56.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 112 billion still available for this year.

asr-003155
02:04:57.060 --> 02:05:02.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is the totality, Your Honor, that includes the 39 billion in NRIP fund.

asr-003156
02:05:02.380 --> 02:05:02.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003157
02:05:03.460 --> 02:05:03.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

asr-003158
02:05:03.860 --> 02:05:07.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So it's the last quarter.

asr-003159
02:05:09.020 --> 02:05:15.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We can make that declaration and we have the funds to provide for the support.

asr-003160
02:05:15.340 --> 02:05:15.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-003161
02:05:17.100 --> 02:05:18.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So thank you.

asr-003162
02:05:18.420 --> 02:05:20.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you for that clarification.

asr-003163
02:05:22.580 --> 02:05:24.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The other one would be the...

asr-003164
02:05:24.640 --> 02:05:26.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I also raised this with the DBM.

asr-003165
02:05:26.720 --> 02:05:28.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I just want an update.

asr-003166
02:05:28.520 --> 02:05:30.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You don't have to answer it now, but if you can, good.

asr-003167
02:05:31.020 --> 02:05:32.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If not, just before plenary.

asr-003168
02:05:32.860 --> 02:05:39.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This is on the funding of the Anti-Agri-Economic Sabotage Council.

asr-003169
02:05:40.200 --> 02:05:43.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We wrote you on last week or two weeks ago.

asr-003170
02:05:46.280 --> 02:05:48.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We emailed you requesting information.

asr-003171
02:05:48.420 --> 02:05:50.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Information on the funding.

asr-003172
02:05:51.280 --> 02:05:52.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Of course, you replied.

asr-003173
02:05:52.640 --> 02:05:53.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

asr-003174
02:05:54.080 --> 02:06:01.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: An initial 500 million was provided under RA 12022, which was establishing the council.

asr-003175
02:06:02.480 --> 02:06:11.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You have identified 35.744 million under OPSF 2025 Presidential Oversight Program.

asr-003176
02:06:11.980 --> 02:06:16.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But it remained unobligated as of August 27, 2026.

asr-003177
02:06:17.020 --> 02:06:17.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But was available.

asr-003178
02:06:18.420 --> 02:06:20.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: For obligation.

asr-003179
02:06:20.760 --> 02:06:22.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It is actually until December 31.

asr-003180
02:06:22.880 --> 02:06:24.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So could you clarify?

asr-003181
02:06:24.640 --> 02:06:28.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: From the initial 500 million, this is what came from?

asr-003182
02:06:29.260 --> 02:06:41.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the reason why I'm raising this is because I had spoken with Deputy Executive Secretary Andres.

asr-003183
02:06:41.680 --> 02:06:47.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And he informed me that for the council to be effective, he needs...

asr-003184
02:06:48.420 --> 02:06:50.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: He needs more people.

asr-003185
02:06:51.380 --> 02:06:53.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But 35 million will not do it.

asr-003186
02:06:55.520 --> 02:06:57.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Actually, Your Honor, if I may respond.

asr-003187
02:06:57.580 --> 02:07:08.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The DBM has already approved the request of the AAES to establish its permanent secretariat.

asr-003188
02:07:08.280 --> 02:07:13.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: They have already issued the necessary approval to the OP.

asr-003189
02:07:13.360 --> 02:07:16.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And I believe they are now organizing the permanent secretariat.

asr-003193
02:07:18.400 --> 02:07:22.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The funding for which is usually sourced from the Miscellaneous Personal Benefits Fund.

asr-003194
02:07:22.780 --> 02:07:28.660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So this is over and above what was initially quoted, which is the 35.74 million,

asr-003195
02:07:28.820 --> 02:07:32.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is just part of the regular operating budget of the OP.

asr-003196
02:07:32.360 --> 02:07:35.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So with the approval on the creation of the positions, Your Honor,

asr-003197
02:07:35.680 --> 02:07:42.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: once they fill that up, we will be releasing additional allotments to cover the salaries of the hired personnel, Your Honor.

asr-003198
02:07:43.160 --> 02:07:44.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay. Thank you.

asr-003200
02:07:45.320 --> 02:07:47.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because as I mentioned,

asr-003201
02:07:47.040 --> 02:07:53.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: kahapon sa DA budget at sa ilang pagkakataon, pati sa DOA budget,

asr-003202
02:07:54.580 --> 02:07:59.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: yung problema ng smuggling, billion-billion ang nakumpiska.

asr-003203
02:08:00.700 --> 02:08:06.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Itong last month, dalawang shipment ng bigas galing Vietnam,

asr-003204
02:08:06.860 --> 02:08:09.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: totaling about 700 million pesos,

asr-003205
02:08:09.500 --> 02:08:15.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang threshold sa smuggling na non-bailable, yung economic sabotage,

asr-003206
02:08:15.500 --> 02:08:19.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: is only 10 million pesos worth of agriculture products.

asr-003207
02:08:20.320 --> 02:08:25.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero dahil, well, yun yung malaking tanong.

asr-003208
02:08:25.620 --> 02:08:32.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Billion na nakakumpis ka, pero wala pang nakukulong na financier ng daang milyon.

asr-003209
02:08:32.760 --> 02:08:36.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kahit na 10 million lang ang threshold.

asr-003210
02:08:37.260 --> 02:08:41.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So para tayong keystone cops, you know,

asr-003211
02:08:42.240 --> 02:08:44.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: sino bang above 60 dito?

asr-003212
02:08:45.000 --> 02:08:45.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Alam nyo yung...

asr-003213
02:08:45.500 --> 02:08:46.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Keystone cops, di ba?

asr-003214
02:08:46.740 --> 02:08:47.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung mga...

asr-003215
02:08:47.820 --> 02:08:50.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, ang version natin would be polis patola.

asr-003216
02:08:51.080 --> 02:08:51.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No?

asr-003217
02:08:51.640 --> 02:08:54.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kumpiska tayo ng kumpiska, pero yung mga salarin,

asr-003218
02:08:54.640 --> 02:08:57.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: hindi naman natin kinukulong, hindi naman natin kinakasuhan.

asr-003219
02:08:57.980 --> 02:09:02.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So this AAES funding is critical

asr-003220
02:09:02.600 --> 02:09:08.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so that we can pinapatay ng smuggling yung ating local farmers

asr-003221
02:09:08.560 --> 02:09:10.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and fisher folk, no?

asr-003222
02:09:12.040 --> 02:09:13.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, okay.

asr-003223
02:09:14.380 --> 02:09:15.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Siguro yung huli natin,

asr-003224
02:09:15.500 --> 02:09:18.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: just going back to the earlier LGSF,

asr-003225
02:09:19.480 --> 02:09:22.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: you know, I remember kasi during the time of Secretary Butchabad,

asr-003226
02:09:22.960 --> 02:09:26.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: they were strong, and Secretary Jesse Robredo,

asr-003227
02:09:26.820 --> 02:09:29.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: they were very strong on the bottoms-up budgeting.

asr-003228
02:09:32.240 --> 02:09:42.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that a program that the DBM is considering, you know, to reintroduce?

asr-003229
02:09:43.340 --> 02:09:45.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Your Honor, actually, there is one...

asr-003230
02:09:45.500 --> 02:09:47.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: There is one sub-program under the LGSF,

asr-003231
02:09:48.000 --> 02:09:51.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is what we call the Support for Participatory Budgeting,

asr-003232
02:09:51.800 --> 02:09:55.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: although it's only 1 billion out of the total LGSF.

asr-003233
02:09:55.420 --> 02:10:01.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So we intend to use this really to also incentivize public participation,

asr-003234
02:10:01.700 --> 02:10:03.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: CSO participation in the budget.

asr-003235
02:10:03.520 --> 02:10:09.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And for 2027, this is also one thing that we would like to use

asr-003236
02:10:09.880 --> 02:10:13.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to incentivize LGUs who have actively...

asr-003237
02:10:15.500 --> 02:10:17.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Participated in the Open Government Partnership,

asr-003238
02:10:17.760 --> 02:10:21.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: almost similar to the concept of the bottom-up budgeting implemented before, Your Honor.

asr-003239
02:10:22.160 --> 02:10:26.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, and if you can provide us, you know, some material on this

asr-003240
02:10:26.860 --> 02:10:32.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so that we can, likewise, you know, if we need to fund more, why not?

asr-003241
02:10:32.620 --> 02:10:33.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Certainly, Your Honor.

asr-003242
02:10:34.720 --> 02:10:37.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, on the issue of the...

asr-003243
02:10:37.260 --> 02:10:38.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What's the term again?

asr-003244
02:10:38.240 --> 02:10:41.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The 23 billion that was allocated for rice?

asr-003245
02:10:42.300 --> 02:10:43.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Under the Falgo, Your Honor.

asr-003246
02:10:43.740 --> 02:10:44.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, I sat...

asr-003247
02:10:45.500 --> 02:10:49.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Down with Secretary ES, Recto,

asr-003248
02:10:49.400 --> 02:10:53.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and actually in the memorandum circular that you issued

asr-003249
02:10:53.560 --> 02:10:57.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: or that the ES issued on the 23 billion,

asr-003250
02:10:57.600 --> 02:11:02.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: there was a provision there on encouraging Sagip Saka, no?

asr-003251
02:11:03.220 --> 02:11:10.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But I've been hearing that there are some LGUs that buy the imported rice, no?

asr-003252
02:11:11.700 --> 02:11:13.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: For some reason, no?

asr-003253
02:11:14.820 --> 02:11:15.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-003254
02:11:15.460 --> 02:11:15.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat yun.

asr-003255
02:11:16.140 --> 02:11:16.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bawal.

asr-003256
02:11:18.420 --> 02:11:20.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Certainly, Your Honor, there is...

asr-003257
02:11:22.360 --> 02:11:26.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the understanding that really, there is an express...

asr-003258
02:11:26.860 --> 02:11:29.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We're just verifying, Your Honor, if there is an express prohibition,

asr-003259
02:11:29.780 --> 02:11:30.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but we are of the understanding...

asr-003260
02:11:30.240 --> 02:11:31.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No, there is no prohibition.

asr-003261
02:11:31.820 --> 02:11:34.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That we highly encourage...

asr-003262
02:11:34.780 --> 02:11:39.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No, there is no prohibition on imported rice, number one.

asr-003263
02:11:39.560 --> 02:11:43.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Number two, it only encourages, di ba,

asr-003264
02:11:43.420 --> 02:11:43.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: that the fund be...

asr-003265
02:11:43.560 --> 02:11:44.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That the fund be...

asr-003266
02:11:45.460 --> 02:11:47.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Utilized to purchase directly.

asr-003267
02:11:47.840 --> 02:11:48.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To purchase Sagip Saka, yun.

asr-003268
02:11:48.860 --> 02:11:49.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, yes.

asr-003269
02:11:49.860 --> 02:11:52.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's important because, you know,

asr-003270
02:11:53.460 --> 02:11:57.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: case in point is the city government of Quezon City.

asr-003271
02:11:58.880 --> 02:12:01.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And this was explained to me by Joy Belmonte.

asr-003272
02:12:01.460 --> 02:12:05.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They bought about 200 plus million worth of rice

asr-003273
02:12:05.980 --> 02:12:09.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: directly sa farmers and Fisherfolk Cooperative

asr-003274
02:12:09.540 --> 02:12:11.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: using the LGSF fund.

asr-003275
02:12:11.200 --> 02:12:11.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The rice...

asr-003276
02:12:12.760 --> 02:12:13.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What's the name?

asr-003277
02:12:14.080 --> 02:12:15.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Bawat bayan makikinawa...

asr-003278
02:12:15.460 --> 02:12:15.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-003279
02:12:16.140 --> 02:12:17.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And she told me,

asr-003280
02:12:18.420 --> 02:12:20.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: if they went through the regular bidding process,

asr-003281
02:12:20.900 --> 02:12:25.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: it would have been about 15 pesos per kilo more expensive.

asr-003282
02:12:27.160 --> 02:12:29.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They got it at 50 pesos per kilo

asr-003283
02:12:29.400 --> 02:12:31.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: when they bought it directly from the farmers' co-op.

asr-003284
02:12:32.240 --> 02:12:34.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But if it went through the public bidding,

asr-003285
02:12:34.500 --> 02:12:36.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: it would have been about 65 pesos a kilo.

asr-003286
02:12:36.820 --> 02:12:40.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So they saved over 100 plus million pesos worth

asr-003287
02:12:40.180 --> 02:12:42.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: of LGSF funds.

asr-003288
02:12:44.060 --> 02:12:45.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And they were able to buy...

asr-003289
02:12:45.460 --> 02:12:49.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, it works if it's made to work.

asr-003290
02:12:50.660 --> 02:12:52.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, I hope, you know,

asr-003291
02:12:52.780 --> 02:12:55.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and the discussion was towards being able to provide,

asr-003292
02:12:55.980 --> 02:12:59.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: you know, incentives for our local governments

asr-003293
02:12:59.340 --> 02:13:00.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: to do the same.

asr-003294
02:13:00.380 --> 02:13:03.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, hopefully, as you implement this program

asr-003295
02:13:03.300 --> 02:13:05.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: together with the LGUs,

asr-003296
02:13:06.340 --> 02:13:10.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: is there a interagency committee that oversees this?

asr-003297
02:13:11.500 --> 02:13:12.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How does that work?

asr-003298
02:13:12.620 --> 02:13:13.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Right now, Your Honor,

asr-003299
02:13:13.720 --> 02:13:15.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we are working with the DILG,

asr-003300
02:13:15.460 --> 02:13:19.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the monitoring of the actual implementation of the program.

asr-003301
02:13:20.060 --> 02:13:23.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, the DILG shares their monitoring reports back to the DBM

asr-003302
02:13:23.900 --> 02:13:26.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: about the status of the LGSF fund.

asr-003303
02:13:26.120 --> 02:13:28.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, your LGSF fund will go...

asr-003304
02:13:29.120 --> 02:13:32.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know, what is 15 pesos or 50 pesos?

asr-003305
02:13:32.520 --> 02:13:33.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How much percent is that?

asr-003306
02:13:33.980 --> 02:13:34.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that...

asr-003307
02:13:35.440 --> 02:13:37.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, your fund will...

asr-003308
02:13:38.640 --> 02:13:41.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You're extending your fund 30% more

asr-003309
02:13:41.680 --> 02:13:43.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: if you implement it correctly.

asr-003310
02:13:43.680 --> 02:13:45.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And these are not small amounts.

asr-003311
02:13:45.460 --> 02:13:48.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The PIDIG Multipurpose Cooperative

asr-003312
02:13:48.860 --> 02:13:52.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: sold 52 million pesos worth of rice.

asr-003313
02:13:52.840 --> 02:13:55.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Another cooperative, San Peregrina.

asr-003314
02:13:56.340 --> 02:13:58.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Meron palang San Peregrin.

asr-003315
